@tradition garden-walk
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 7(a), week 9 (FX17's shape: Sunday morning, the garden or the promenade). Garden walk: every 8 weeks
// from Day 63, after Slow stretch (08:00-08:45); 09:15 since RV14 (FX17: the host was still at breakfast at 08:45). Tove Cruz (they/them) leads a slow walk round the garden and names
// every bed by the week it was sown; you may pick one leaf to taste. Cruz hosts.
k: 716
title: Garden walk
when: every 8 weeks sunday week 1 from day 57
at: 09:15-10:00
min: 20
where: 3 pool garden
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
hold: none
who: cruz-tove always, gardener 70%, garden-lover 60%, early-riser 30%, everyone 8%
anim: talk
host: cruz-tove
from: cruz-tove
invite: host=cruz-tove odds=25% line="Garden walk. Sunday, early. I'll show you the week-nine beans. They're lovely."

== mail
- Garden walk tomorrow, {time}. A slow lap of the garden, every bed and the week it was sown. One leaf each to taste. Not the chillies.

== ask
- Garden walk this morning. Cruz knows every plant by its week.
- Coming on the garden walk? Bring your slow feet.   #funny

== here
- That's a week-four lettuce, apparently. Lovely age.
- Don't touch the chillies. Just don't.   #funny
- Smell the basil. Go on.

== thanks
- Cruz leads a slow walk round the garden, naming every bed by the week it was sown. You get one leaf to taste.   #warm

== chatter
- Cruz knew the week every bed was sown. Every one.
- Garden walk this morning. I tasted a leaf. I'm a changed person.   #funny
- Nicest way to start a Sunday, that walk.   #warm
